                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.date.enforcement_date" : [ {
                  "value" : "05-07-2013",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.date.issued" : [ {
                  "value" : "2013-09-10",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.date.last_modified" : [ {
                  "value" : "2019-12-02",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
                  "value" : "Summary of The National Food Security Act, 2013 \nKey Provisions\nI. Core Entitlements\n1.\tSubsidised Foodgrains: - Priority Households: 5 kg/person/month at subsidised rates.\n•\tAntyodaya Anna Yojana Households: Up to 35 kg/household/month, covering 75% rural and 50% urban population.\n2.\tNutritional Support: - Pregnant & Lactating Mothers: Free meals and ₹6,000 maternity benefit.\n•\tChildren:\n•\t0-6 years: Meals through anganwadi.\n•\t6-14 years: Mid-day meals in schools.\n•\tMalnourished Children: Free meals through anganwadi.\nII. Agricultural Development for Food Security\n1.\tFarmer Support: - Increased agricultural investments.\n•\tRemunerative prices and access to inputs, credit, and insurance.\n•\tProhibition on unwarranted diversion of agricultural land and water.\n2.\tSupply Chain Enhancements: - Decentralised procurement, including coarse grains.\n•\tModern, decentralised storage facilities.\n•\tPriority to foodgrain movement with enhanced railway capacity.\nIII. Social Welfare & Access\n1.\tBasic Amenities: - Access to safe drinking water and sanitation.\n•\tUniversal healthcare access.\n2.\tVulnerable Groups: - Nutritional, health, and education support for adolescent girls.\n•\tPensions for senior citizens, persons with disability, and single women.\nIV. Special & Administrative Provisions\n1.\tVulnerable Areas: - Special focus on food security in remote, hilly, and tribal areas.\n2.\tImplementation & Oversight:\n•\tPower to Address Difficulties: Central Government can issue orders to resolve implementation challenges within 2 years.\n•\tInstitutional Flexibility: Utilize established authorities for other schemes.\n•\tForce Majeure: Exemption from liability in extraordinary circumstances (war, natural disasters).\n•\tRepeal and Savings: Continuity of actions and rights from the repealed Ordinance.",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.act_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "AC_CEN_21_28_000010_201320_1517807327638",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
